Z||000000||Fiero*101||08-26-2001||02:52 AM||||ok my major problem is my throttle cable its streched well at least thats what the guy told me when i bought it. If you put your foot into it Gos but you have to floor it but then its Floored and i dont like to beat on my car to get it up to speed so i was wondering has any body ever changed a throttle cable? if So i would be more then greatful if you could tell me how to do it.<P>my Oil leaks from the pan you can just see it drip from the pan. any ideas how to fix that?<BR>My anitfreeze leaks out some how thru little hoses going from the big hose it looks like to the manifold but i tightend them but it still leaks any ideas?<P>ok my next one im hoping can be fixed easy its my gas gage i hope it just needs replaced for some reason i dont get very good gas miliage. what could the cause of that be?<P>my enigine service light comes on about 15 to 20 min of just strait driving for now reason at all and will stay on till i turn off the key. any ideas on that one?<P>Ok sorry guys last one<BR>My voltmeter light stays on after i turn the key, but shuts off about 10 seconds later is this a problem my dad thought it is b/c he was like "It shouldnt stay on after you turn the key" any ideas on that one? <P>Ok i think thats all my problems that i can think of Sorry it was so long but I LOVE MY CAR! and i want all my problems fixed asap so i can enjoy my car w/ out worrying about it<P>thanks again<BR>Fiero*101<P>1986 Gold SE 2M6<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Dr.Hancock||||reg||1
Z||000001||8Ball||08-26-2001||03:25 AM||||Ok first the oil leak, You will need to replace the gasket for the oil pan very easy and very quick to do.<BR>Second the coolant leaks, Sounds like your hoses are dry rotted. would be a VERY good Idea to replace those.<BR>Third the Gas Gauge.<BR>Well the gas gauge has nothing to do with the milage you get. It mearly displays how much gas is in your tank.<BR>I would say for better milage and from the sounds of the rest of your probs you need a full tune up. New plugs, plug wires, distributer cap and button for starters.<BR>While your at it, (and no it won't really help your milage but the car prolly needs it) Change the oil and flush the coolant after you replace the hoses.<P>Hope that helps ya somewhat<P><BR>P.S. I too just brought an 86 gold 2m6 from the dead  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Bought it out of a junkyard/carlot for 800 bucks and put another 600 into it. Stiull working on it some but for the most part runs great and will smoke a muskrat...err mustang<p>[This message has been edited by 8Ball (edited 08-26-2001).]||||reg||1
